Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-21-2001||09:21 PM||||I refurbished all my vinyl parts that were curling.  I took them off, removed all the foam crap that had come off with acetone (be careful, can melt the vinyl) and used super glue to glue the covering back to the plastic frame.  I used a spray super glue accelerator, takes the total cure time of super glue down to about 4 seconds.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||03-22-2001||12:52 AM||||I use paint stir sticks (for a straight edge), clamps and super glue -- I have repaired and refurbished all of the vinyl parts on my three GT's and on many customers cars that way.........it can be done.....||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||03-22-2001||09:54 PM||||I always thought it would be a good idea for some fiero business to make shift consoles... it seems every fiero I see has one in bad shape.  (Maybe carbon fiber??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
